Small Tall Cell is a folder which contains a supercell which is:

n1 = 2;  
n2 = 2;
n3 = 40;

at layer n3 = 32, there is one indium atom. With 4 cations present in this layerthis makes a 25% layer. This cell was made to 
test supercell size effects and give insight into other DFT results.

Small Small Cell is a folder which contains a supercell which is:

n1 = 2;
n2 = 2;
n3 = 20;

This directory is to now test vertical localisation of the electron wave function. In our TB calculations we 
get the electron localised to the monolayer. But some dft calculations do not get this, they get the electron 
wave funciton spread out. Thus we here lower the vertical extent of our supercell to see if supercell size effects 
delocalise our electron. If this happens then we know the DFT results are bad due to out of plane delocalisation 
caused by insufficiently large supercell.

In configurations, we have monolayer 25% supercells of size 64,64,40 with no WWF
Seed = Config number
Indium Content = 25
well starts at nz = 32
well ends at nz = 32
wwf is false
well width fluctuation starts at  = 0
well width fluctuation ends at = 0

In configurations_Withwwfs we have 25% supercells of size 64,64,40:
Seed = Config Number
Indium Content = 25
well starts at nz = 32
well ends at nz = 32
wwf is true
well width fluctuation starts at  = 31
well width fluctuation ends at = 31
